  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Nominations: two patterns",
   "texto": [
    "The infinitives can be substantive: **das Entscheiden**, **das Verkaufen**, **das Wohnen**; they are written with capital and are neutral. Other names are lexic derivatives with own gender and meaning: **die Entscheidung**, **der Verkauf**, **die Wohnung**. Do not doubt that all the derivative nouns are equivalent to infinitive: learn gender and use with each word."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Adjectives and verbalization",
   "texto": [
    "Some adjectives form names (**frei → die Freiheit**, **gesund → die Gesundheit**), but the form is not always predictable. To return to a verbal sentence, he identifies who does the action and turns the name into his verb: **nach dem Verkauf des Hauses** → **nachdem man das Haus verkauft hat**. The choice of time depends on the context."
   ]
  },
